Pin the "Users cannot set <ban|kick|redact> powerlevel higher than their own"
tests to a pre-v12 room version.

These tests were written for the pre-v12 semantics where the room creator holds
an explicit finite power level (100): step 2 sets ban/kick/redact to 10000000
and expects a 403 because that exceeds the creator's own level. Since sytest
#1429 (2026-08-03) made TEST_ROOM_VERSION default to '12', the tests now run in
room v12 (MSC4289), where the room creator's power is effectively infinite and
the spec's "If the new value is higher than the sender's current power level,
reject" rule does not block a finite value like 10000000 — the reference
implementations (Synapse CREATOR_POWER_LEVEL = 2^53, gomatrixserverlib
CreatorPowerLevel = 2^53) both accept it, and sytest never exercises these
tests against them (the can_change_power_levels capability is only proved by
the katrix-side unmask patch). The tests' intent is pre-v12 creator semantics,
so pin them to room version 11, mirroring how sytest #1429 itself pinned
30rooms/60version_upgrade.pl ("/upgrade ...") to v11 for the identical reason
(infinite creator power). The sibling "notifications powerlevel" test already
pins room_version => "6" for the same reason.

If this stops applying against a newer sytest develop, rebase it (the hunk is
in stable, old test code).

--- a/tests/30rooms/08levels.pl
+++ b/tests/30rooms/08levels.pl
@@ -141,7 +141,7 @@
 foreach my $levelname (qw( ban kick redact )) {
    multi_test "Users cannot set $levelname powerlevel higher than their own",
-      requires => [ $creator_fixture, $user_fixture, lockeddown_room_fixture(),
+      requires => [ $creator_fixture, $user_fixture, lockeddown_room_fixture( room_version => "11" ),
                     qw( can_change_power_levels )],
 
       do => sub {
